# Privacy Policy for ShopLiNote

**Effective date:** October 28, 2026

**Last updated:** October 28, 2026

## 1. Introduction

This Privacy Policy explains how ShopLiNote (“the App”) handles information when you use the application.

ShopLiNote is developed and maintained by GALYAMINSKY. If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact us at **galyaminsky@gmail.com**.

By using ShopLiNote, you acknowledge the practices described in this Privacy Policy.

## 2. Information Stored on Your Device

ShopLiNote is designed to store its main content locally on your device. This content may include:

- Notes and shopping lists.
- Items and quantities within shopping lists.
- Entries in the App’s item library.
- App preferences, such as theme, date format, and text display settings.

The App does not require you to create an account. The inspected version does not provide developer-operated cloud storage or account-based synchronization of your notes and shopping lists.

Local storage does not necessarily mean that information can never leave your device. Android system backup and device-transfer features may copy eligible app data, depending on the Android version, device configuration, backup service, and your settings.

## 3. Analytics and Third-Party Services

ShopLiNote uses **Firebase Analytics**, a service provided by Google, to understand how the App is used and to help improve its functionality and reliability.

Depending on the SDK configuration and applicable platform settings, analytics information may include:

- App interactions and automatically collected app events.
- App launches, sessions, and usage information.
- App version and update information.
- Device model, operating system, and related technical information.
- An app-instance identifier used for analytics.
- General geographic information that may be inferred by Google from network information.

Firebase Analytics may automatically collect certain events and technical information even when the App does not explicitly log custom analytics events.

The App also uses Google Play Services and other libraries required for its Android functionality. Information processed by these services is subject to the relevant providers’ documentation and privacy practices.

**Advertising ID:** The App is configured to disable Advertising ID collection by Firebase Analytics. This does not necessarily disable every Google attribution mechanism or prevent every third-party service from processing other technical identifiers. The App does not include the Google Mobile Ads SDK in this version and does not display AdMob advertisements.

Google’s privacy information is available at:

- [Google Privacy Policy](https://policies.google.com/privacy)
- [Firebase Privacy and Security](https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy)
- [Firebase Analytics data collection](https://firebase.google.com/docs/analytics)

## 4. How Information Is Used

Information processed by ShopLiNote and its analytics service may be used to:

- Provide the App’s core functionality.
- Save and display your notes, shopping lists, and preferences.
- Understand general usage patterns.
- Identify technical issues and improve app performance.
- Maintain and improve the App.

The developer does not use the App’s local notes and shopping-list content for advertising purposes through an integrated advertising SDK.

## 5. Sharing Information

ShopLiNote does not provide a developer-operated cloud service for synchronizing or storing your notes and shopping lists.

Analytics information may be transmitted to and processed by Google through Firebase Analytics in accordance with Google’s applicable terms and privacy documentation.

The App also provides a sharing function. If you choose to share a shopping list, the selected content is passed to the Android sharing interface and the application you select. The recipient application’s handling of that information is governed by its own privacy policy and practices.

Android system backup or device-transfer services may process eligible local app data as described in Section 2.

The developer does not sell your personal information.

## 6. Data Retention and Deletion

Your notes, shopping lists, item-library entries, and preferences are stored in the App’s local data storage. You can generally remove this local data by clearing the App’s storage through Android settings or by uninstalling the App. These actions may permanently remove local information.

If Android backup or device-transfer features have copied eligible data, copies may remain subject to the relevant system or backup service’s retention and restoration behavior.

Analytics data is processed and retained by Google under the applicable Firebase Analytics configuration and Google policies. Retention periods may depend on service settings. The developer does not claim to be able to identify or individually delete every analytics record associated with a device or app instance.

For additional information about Google’s handling of analytics data, consult the Firebase documentation linked above.

## 7. Data Security

ShopLiNote uses Android’s application storage mechanisms for local data. However, no storage method or electronic transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

You are responsible for securing access to your device and reviewing its backup, transfer, and application-permission settings.

## 8. Children’s Privacy

ShopLiNote is not intended to collect personal information directly from children through an account-registration system. The App does not require an account.

Because Firebase Analytics may process technical and usage information, parents or guardians should review the relevant Google and Firebase privacy documentation when considering the App’s use by children.

If you believe that information has been handled inappropriately in connection with the App, contact us at **galyaminsky@gmail.com**.

## 9. External Services and Links

The App may rely on Google Play Services, Firebase Analytics, Android system features, and applications selected by you for sharing content. These services may be governed by separate terms and privacy policies.

The developer is not responsible for the independent privacy practices of third-party services or applications.

## 10. Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated when the App’s functionality, data practices, or applicable requirements change.

The revised version will display an updated effective date. You should review the policy periodically to remain informed about how information is handled.

